WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Here is an eighteen-word skill for extractive question answering:

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.324
Use only the supplied context,

3
00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:10.200
and return the shortest span that answers the question.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.297
With a minimal harness,

5
00:00:12.347 --> 00:00:16.300
it raises exact match on SQuAD by sixty-six points.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.814
Now give the agent a richer harness.

7
00:00:18.864 --> 00:00:22.120
What happens to the skill's gain? Take a guess.

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.690
The answer is...

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.480
now it adds just two points.

10
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.840
So, is it a good skill?

11
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.607
We usually credit a skill with one number: accuracy with it,

12
00:00:35.657 --> 00:00:37.650
minus accuracy without it.

13
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.181
Yet the same skill just got two very different numbers:

14
00:00:41.231 --> 00:00:42.670
sixty-six and two.

15
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.227
That number belongs to the harness as much as to the skill.

16
00:00:47.277 --> 00:00:51.079
The harness is everything that runs the agent around the model:

17
00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:55.220
the answer interface, error feedback, retries, and reflection.

18
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.134
So we ask:

19
00:00:56.184 --> 00:01:00.200
under which harness does a skill become real capability?

20
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.607
To find out, we freeze the model and the skill,

21
00:01:04.657 --> 00:01:07.420
and climb the harness one level at a time.

22
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.441
We test four skill conditions: no skill, a Direct skill,

23
00:01:12.491 --> 00:01:16.920
SkillOpt, and Trace2Skill, on nine benchmarks, three runs each.

24
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.836
So what did we find? First, skill value moves with the harness,

25
00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:23.090
in three ways.

26
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.708
One: absorbed. With a minimal harness,

27
00:01:25.758 --> 00:01:29.120
the skill adds sixty-six points; with a richer harness,

28
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.130
only two, because the harness already does the skill's job.

29
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.647
Two: rescued. Without error feedback,

30
00:01:35.697 --> 00:01:39.093
the skill costs twenty-two points; feed the errors back,

31
00:01:39.143 --> 00:01:41.720
and the loss turns into a small gain.

32
00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.043
Three: preserved.

33
00:01:43.093 --> 00:01:46.702
The skill adds about thirteen points under both harnesses,

34
00:01:46.752 --> 00:01:50.270
because it fixes a failure that no harness can see.

35
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.476
Finding two: where does recovery break?

36
00:01:53.526 --> 00:01:57.270
It works mainly when the failure leaves a visible signal.

37
00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.898
We sort the failures into two classes:

38
00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:01.643
those with a visible signal,

39
00:02:01.693 --> 00:02:04.573
such as a format violation or an error message,

40
00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:06.567
and those with no signal at all,

41
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:09.410
just a wrong answer that raises nothing.

42
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:15.212
Then we count how many the richer harness rescues on three question-answering benchmarks.

43
00:02:15.262 --> 00:02:17.250
With a signal, almost half.

44
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.250
Without one, about two in a hundred.

45
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.544
Finding three: run both models on twenty labeled tasks,

46
00:02:24.594 --> 00:02:28.150
and switch to the stronger model only where it wins.

47
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.642
This pilot beats always using GPT-5.6-sol:

48
00:02:31.692 --> 00:02:35.733
fifty-seven point four versus fifty-three point five,

49
00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:38.630
at thirty-six percent lower cost.

50
00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.193
The same holds for both Sonnet models: higher scores,

51
00:02:42.243 --> 00:02:44.550
and about forty percent cheaper.

52
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.065
To sum up: we froze the model and the skill,

53
00:02:48.115 --> 00:02:51.080
and climbed the harness one level at a time.

54
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.300
First, skill value moves with the harness.

55
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:54.788
Second,

56
00:02:54.838 --> 00:02:59.080
recovery works mainly when the failure leaves a visible signal.

57
00:02:59.170 --> 00:02:59.509
Third,

58
00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:03.792
a small pilot per benchmark beats always using the stronger model,

59
00:03:03.842 --> 00:03:04.750
at lower cost.

